FAQ
Questions people actually ask
Can I use another computer instead of a Raspberry Pi 5?
Yes. The install script runs on any 64-bit machine with Ubuntu, Debian or another Debian-based Linux, Intel/AMD or ARM, from an old PC to a mini PC, with 8 GB of memory, and gives you the same app. The ready-made image, the setup over Bluetooth, the status lights and the alerts that name a USB port are the Raspberry Pi 5's.
What does it cost?
The software is free and open source: you buy the Pi, its card, two drives, a power supply and a cooler once, and at home it needs nothing else. To reach it from outside your home, the bridge is free for its first two years, then €9.99 + VAT a year with up to five addresses.
Can I reach it when I'm away from home?
Yes: the bridge gives your device an address like casa.off-the.cloud, which the apps use whenever you're out, and your friends' devices reach it there. At home the apps connect straight to the device, at the speed of your own network.
How does it stay up to date?
When a new release is out, the device says so in its alerts, and Update in Settings installs it: the device checks the release against the project's signature, builds it and restarts. Your photos and files stay where they are.
